{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And He charged Joshua son of Nun</b> — this is turned upward, toward the Shekhinah, as is explicit in 'to the land concerning which I swore to them' and 'and I will be with you' — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 31:23). And he interpreted well. According to the opinion of R. Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Deuteronomy 31:15), 'and He charged Joshua' means Moses charged him by the commandment of HaShem, and therefore it says 'which I swore to them.' And so we find that Moses said, 'and I will give the rain of your land in its season' (Deuteronomy 11:14), and likewise 'and I will give grass in your field for your cattle' (ibid. verse 15), and likewise 'that you may know that I am YHWH your Elohim' (Deuteronomy 29:5), and likewise 'YHWH will send upon you the curse because of the evil of your deeds in that you have forsaken Me' (Deuteronomy 28:20), and I have already spoken about these (Ramban on Deuteronomy 5:12)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:57:54.657196377Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}